-- title:
--   Invariance of y under translations by q'^{-j}
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $R$ and $q'$ with $R$ nonzero, assume $q'$ is prime and does not divide $R$, and fix a weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$. Let $y$ be a cusp form of weight $k$ for the image in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_0(R) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. The hypothesis on $y$ is that the slashed function $y \mid_k \delta$, where $\delta =$ `heckeDiagMatrix` $q'$ is the invertible upper triangular matrix $\begin{pmatrix} q' & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$ (the definition returns the identity when the index is $0$, which does not occur here), is itself invariant under the weight-$k$ slash action of every element $\gamma$ of that image of $\Gamma_0(R)$: $(y \mid_k \delta) \mid_k \gamma = y \mid_k \delta$ as functions on the upper half-plane. The conclusion is that for every natural number $j$ and every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$ one has $y\bigl((q'^{j})^{-1} +\!\!{}_{\mathrm v}\, \tau\bigr) = y(\tau)$, i.e. $y$ is invariant under translation by the real number $q'^{-j}$.
--
--   This is the analytic input of Ihara's lemma in the form used by Ribet: a cusp form on $\Gamma_0(R)$ whose twist by $\mathrm{diag}(q',1)$ is again $\Gamma_0(R)$-invariant is invariant under the group generated by $\Gamma_0(R)$ and its $\delta$-conjugate, which by the Serre–Ihara amalgam decomposition of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[1/q'])$ contains all unipotents $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & q'^{-j} \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$; accordingly the proof invokes the surjectivity statement [`Ihara.amalgamToGamma0Away_surjective`](thm.html#Ihara.amalgamToGamma0Away_surjective). It is used to deduce the vanishing results [`CuspForm.eq_zero_of_coe_add_slash_heckeDiagMatrix_eq_zero`](thm.html#CuspForm.eq_zero_of_coe_add_slash_heckeDiagMatrix_eq_zero) and [`CuspForm.eq_zero_of_slash_heckeDiagMatrix_slash_eq_of_mem_Gamma1`](thm.html#CuspForm.eq_zero_of_slash_heckeDiagMatrix_slash_eq_of_mem_Gamma1), the injectivity half of Ihara's lemma.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_vadd_inv_pow_eq_of_slash_heckeDiagMatrix_invariant.lean

